<title>USA: Marathon raises most posted crude prices.</title>
<headline>Marathon raises most posted crude prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it had raised the price it will pay for most U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Tuesday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.75 a barrel. West Texas Sour was left unchanged at $16.90 a barrel.</p>
<p>The Light Louisiana sweet crude price was raised to $19.00 and Oklahoma sweet was raised to $18.75.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
